  "notes": [
    "M5.0 uses the public Switchboard On-Demand devnet queue for draw and election randomness.",
    "The queue PDA is documented for SDK/on-chain verification context; GlobalConfig stores the queue address for both VRF config fields.",
    "Tokenomics Core proposal 9 and campaign migration proposal 10 were executed through the existing 2-of-3 Squads governance on devnet.",
    "JDR campaign 0 is active under the v2 economic hash. The migration changed only the economic configuration hash and moved no tokens.",
    "Tokenomics Core proposal 14 deployed the cancellable Treasury SOL Vault budget artifact. Wallet A and Wallet B approvals were operated from one local `.env`, satisfying the on-chain threshold without independent human review; no treasury SOL or JDR moved during the upgrade.",
    "Tyche proposal 12 shipped the prize-vault solvency fix: `record_claim` reserves each payout against the turn vault, and `sweep_prize_rollover` moves a closed turn's leftover lamports into the open turn's vault so a rolled-over pool is actually payable.",
    "Tyche proposal 13 added `expire_claim`, which releases a payout past its claim window back into its vault's unreserved balance so an abandoned claim cannot pin a turn's pool forever.",
    "Tyche proposal 15 temporarily bridged ProgramData authority to Wallet A. One atomic transaction then extended capacity by 65,536 bytes, funded 456,130,560 rent lamports, and returned authority to Squads vault 0; the deployed binary remained unchanged.",
    "Tyche proposal 19 deployed the corrective fee-pool CPI artifact. Wallet A and Wallet B approved, Wallet B executed, buffer 3uDPkjbohqDncQY6yEVn1N8bXs5XnGaP4YbGcc531QvE closed and refunded its rent to Wallet B, and upgrade authority remains Squads vault 0. Fee-pool migration proposal 18 was then re-simulated successfully and executed by Wallet A: all 23,000,000 legacy lamports moved from Tyche custody into the Tokenomics distribution vault, split into 18,000,000 attributed-unbridged lamports and 5,000,000 rollover lamports, with no JDR movement.",
    "Tokenomics Core proposal 16 deployed the direct-fee artifact. Wallet A and Wallet B approved, Wallet B executed, the buffer closed and refunded its rent to Wallet B, and upgrade authority remains Squads vault 0.",
    "No private keys or secret material belong in this file."
  ]
